<section class="band">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">What you get</p>
      <h2>Made for the saddle, not the car.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feat">
      <div>
        <h3>Turn-by-turn voice</h3>
        <p>A warning while there&rsquo;s still room to react, then &ldquo;Now, turn left&rdquo; at the turn. A UK voice you can change in Settings.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Works with no signal</h3>
        <p>Download the map before you box up. Riders have completed whole loops on BridleNav with no phone signal at all.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Every route on one map</h3>
        <p>Colour-coded by how well we know it. Filter to what&rsquo;s within ten miles of you, or search by name.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>See it before you box up</h3>
        <p>A 3D fly-through of the whole route over real terrain, so you know what you&rsquo;re asking of your horse before the trailer is hitched.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Horsebox parking</h3>
        <p>Where to park, with a postcode and a what3words square &mdash; plus height and length restrictions before you tow somewhere you can&rsquo;t turn round.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Hazards called out</h3>
        <p>Road crossings, gates, boggy stretches, and the two houses where the dogs come at the fence. The things a local would tell you.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Warnings that arrive the same week</h3>
        <p>If a gate is padlocked or the bracken has swallowed a path, the warning reaches your app straight away. You don&rsquo;t wait for an update.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Tell us what&rsquo;s wrong</h3>
        <p>Found a locked gate or a turn we got wrong? Report it from the route in about ten seconds. It comes straight to us, and if it stands up it becomes a warning every other rider sees.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
