<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="built">
      <div class="measure">
        <p class="eyebrow">The community map</p>
        <h2 style="margin-block:12px 20px">The map riders build themselves.</h2>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft)">Forty-one routes will never cover the country. The bridleways you ride most are known by you and a handful of others, and they aren&rsquo;t written down anywhere.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:14px">So BridleNav lets you record a ride and send it in. No files to wrestle with &mdash; you ride it, then at home you write the turn-by-turn directions in your own words and mark the gates, the water and the livestock. Those words are what the app reads aloud to the next rider.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:14px">Every submission is read before it goes live. Put your name to it or don&rsquo;t &mdash; that&rsquo;s your choice, and you can trim the start and finish so a route never begins at your own yard.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder">
        <div><span class="step">1st route approved</span><span class="reward">Your name on the route</span><span class="sub">Or stay anonymous, your choice</span></div>
        <div><span class="step">3 routes</span><span class="reward">Trailblazer badge</span><span class="sub">On your Ride Passport</span></div>
        <div><span class="step">5 routes</span><span class="reward">Local Expert</span><span class="sub">Riders can see the routes you know</span></div>
        <div><span class="step">10 routes</span><span class="reward">Founding Contributor</span><span class="sub">The riders who built the map</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

